        {
            "heading": "Crown Focus",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Rulers can set a province as their Crown Focus if they are:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Duke tier or higher",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Not nomadic",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Any of:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Independent",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Vassal duke with 35 realm size",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Vassal king with 55 realm size",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Vassal with republic, merchant republic , or holy order government",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "A crown focus province gains a small bonus to its hidden prosperity value each year, as long as it is not occupied or experiencing an epidemic disease ."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Effects of high prosperity in crown focus provinces",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "A crown focus province that already has a high prosperity level is eligible for special events. These events are more frequent with high stewardship and learning skills."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "At prosperity level 2, a province with a different culture can be converted at the cost 100% of your yearly income. It also converts the province's religion and removes the nomad agitation modifier, if relevant.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "At prosperity level 3, a new Holding slot can be created for 250% of yearly income.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "At prosperity level 3, various positive modifiers can be added to the province:",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "",
                            "Bonus",
                            "Requirements"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Jewish Settlement",
                            "+25% city tax",
                            "Christian, Zoroastrian or Muslim; no \"Expelled the Jews\" modifier; no \"Minority Settlement\" modifier (in the province)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Minority Settlement",
                            "+25% city tax",
                            "not Christian, Zoroastrian or Muslim; no \"Jewish Settlement\" modifier (in the province)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Glorious Monument",
                            "+0.5 Prestige",
                            ""
                        ],
                        [
                            "Merchant Harbor",
                            "+50% galleys",
                            "province is coastal"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Scholar Foundation",
                            "+0.03 military tech points +0.03 cultural tech points +0.03 economic tech points",
                            ""
                        ],
                        [
                            "Great Library",
                            "+25% technology spread rate",
                            ""
                        ],
                        [
                            "Center of worship",
                            "+0.25 Piety +25% temple tax",
                            ""
                        ],
                        [
                            "Logging Company",
                            "-15% build cost -15% build time",
                            "province terrain is forest or jungle"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Ore Mine",
                            "+10% tax -10% build cost",
                            "province terrain is mountain"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Regimental Ground",
                            "+15% levy",
                            ""
                        ]
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "no \"Expelled the Jews\" modifier;"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "no \"Minority Settlement\" modifier (in the province)"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "no \"Jewish Settlement\" modifier (in the province)"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "+0.03 cultural tech points"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "+0.03 economic tech points"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "+25% temple tax"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "-15% build time"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "-10% build cost"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note that the \"Jewish Settlement\" and the \"Minority Settlement\" modifier are basically the same. They are split into two different modifiers just for historical/roleplaying purposes."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Increasing prosperity",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Each province has a hidden prosperity value that can increase in small increments. When it reaches 100/250/500, the prosperity level increases."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Every province has a chance to gain points yearly. The chance increases with owner stewardship skill, owner prosperity bloodline, \"sign of prosperity\" from adulthood rites, heavy rain, great works , or a local trade post . The chance decreases with war (especially being the primary attacker), various province maluses, or tribal government. The amount of this passive increase depends on the terrain , with coastal provinces getting a boost if they contain a city."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The ambition to \"See the Realm Prosper\":"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Enables some flavor events that increase prosperity",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "If peace is successfully maintained for 5 years, the ambition succeeds and adds 35 points to every eligible province in the entire realm (not just demesne!)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Councilors can increase prosperity:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Certain job actions add 6 points when successful:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Marshal: train troops",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Steward: oversee construction",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Spymaster: study technology",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Spiritual: advance cultural technology",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Passive Job flavour events for council members:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Any councilor with 12+ skill and Smart can trigger a \"good at job\" event",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Marshal or steward with 15+ skill can offer to improve capital",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Many peacetime decisions increase prosperity:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Most feasts and festivals add 8 points",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "A completed tournament adds 15 points",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Ancestor Worship can increase prosperity if you wish for economic assistance",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "For defensive pagans, having certain patron deities may increase prosperity",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Other events:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "A fleet returning with loot adds 12 points in your capital. Limited to once every 5 years (unless you change capital).",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Several events from Way of Life , with the Business focus",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Random opportunity to perform charity, if you have a province with a Hospital",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Random opportunity to invest in provincial apothecaries, if you have a Court Physician",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "When a Master Engineer improves your demesne province, prosperity also increases.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Loss of prosperity",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Disease, looting, and sieges can wipe the progress toward the next prosperity level, and sometimes even drop an entire level. Occupation of holdings will often reset the province's prosperity level to 0."
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}